      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I wanted to make some emission intensity/colour changes based on a viseme blend tree for a bot avatar but doesn't seem (easily) possible without a float parameter. :(\nSeems the SDK has an option for viseme parameter only. Maybe just add another option for a float parameter instead?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-27T21:33:09.510Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The viseme-volume as a float would allow avatar creators to use the paramater in blend-trees. \nThe jaw flap 0-100 Int Paramater is not very useful. Even if I created 100 transitions to 100 separate animations, I am still limited in  comparison to a float.\nRegarding performance concerns, this would only occur when the LipSync Mode is set to \"Viseme Paramater + VisemeVolume\" in the Avatar descriptor, and the conversion \ncould occur locally. \nAttached is a simple example of how it could be used.",
